WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.230
You ask your coding agent for one small feature:

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:04.090
a share button.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.090
Seconds later, it's done.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:08.320
It also shares private drafts.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.760
But this folder is governed by a Shape model.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.750
Change the code without updating the model,

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.040
and the check fails.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.400
The agent writes it down:

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.980
the button exports a private draft.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.100
The agreed model forbids that,

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.980
even with the agent's own grant.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.360
The merge stops.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.390
Here the answer is obviously no.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:29.580
The agent fixes the code

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:31.070
to share the published story,

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:32.710
and updates the model to match.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:34.690
If you did want a change,

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:36.490
like sharing drafts with an editor,

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.410
you'd update the model with the code.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:41.130
Shape checks the claims; review keeps them honest.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.990
Shape: architecture you can check in CI.

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:47.550
Install shp, and start with one rule.
